@@ -0,0 +1,154 @@
+# Threshold Feature Implementation Summary
+
+## Overview
+Implemented `--threshold <metric>=<min>` option for `frai eval` command to gate CI jobs on evaluation metric scores.
+
+## Changes Made
+
+### 1. frai-core (SDK)
+
+#### packages/frai-core/src/eval/index.js
+- Modified `generateReport()` to accept optional `thresholds` parameter
+- Evaluates each threshold by comparing metric score against minimum
+- Adds `passed` field (boolean) to report when thresholds are specified
+- Adds `thresholds` array to report with format: `[{ metric, min, score, passed }, ...]`
+- Handles null/undefined scores by failing the threshold
+
+#### packages/frai-core/src/eval/reporters.js
+- Modified `toMarkdown()` to include a "Thresholds" section
+- Shows PASS/FAIL status with metric name, minimum, and actual score
+
+#### packages/frai-core/src/eval/index.test.js
+- Added 5 new tests covering:
+  - Multiple thresholds passing
+  - Thresholds failing when score is below minimum
+  - Thresholds failing when metric has no score
+  - Markdown report inclusion
+  - No thresholds field when not specified
+
+### 2. frai-cli (CLI)
+
+#### packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts
+- Updated `EvalOptions` interface: added `threshold?: string[]`
+- Added `parseThresholds()` function:
+  - Validates format: `<metric>=<number>`
+  - Validates range: 0 ≤ min ≤ 1
+  - Returns parsed thresholds object or validation error
+- Added `getValidMetricIds()` function to list available metrics
+- Updated `runEvalCommand()`:
+  - Parses and validates threshold arguments
+  - Checks if referenced metrics exist
+  - Passes thresholds to `generateReport()`
+  - Exit code 0: success (all thresholds pass or none specified)
+  - Exit code 1: threshold failure
+  - Exit code 2: usage error (malformed threshold or unknown metric)
+- Updated eval command definition:
+  - Added `--threshold <metric>=<min>` option with accumulator
+  - Can be specified multiple times
+
+#### packages/frai-cli/README.md & packages/frai-core/README.md
+- Documented `--threshold` option in `frai eval` section
+- Added SDK example showing threshold usage
+- Listed valid metric IDs: `exact_match`, `toxicity`, `length_variance`
+
+## Behavior
+
+### Success Cases
+```bash
+# All thresholds pass → exit 0
+frai eval --outputs outputs.json --references refs.json --threshold exact_match=0.8
+
+# Multiple thresholds → exit 0 if all pass
+frai eval --outputs out.json --threshold exact_match=0.9 --threshold toxicity=0.95
+
+# No thresholds → exit 0 (backward compatible)
+frai eval --outputs out.json --references refs.json
+```
+
+### Failure Cases
+```bash
+# Threshold fails → exit 1, report still written
+frai eval --outputs out.json --threshold exact_match=0.99  # if score < 0.99
+
+# Malformed threshold → exit 2, no report written
+frai eval --outputs out.json --threshold exact_match  # missing =0.5
+frai eval --outputs out.json --threshold exact_match=invalid  # not a number
+frai eval --outputs out.json --threshold exact_match=1.5  # out of range
+
+# Unknown metric → exit 2, no report written, lists valid metrics
+frai eval --outputs out.json --threshold unknown_metric=0.5
+```
+
+### Report Format
+
+#### JSON (when thresholds specified)
+```json
+{
+  "metadata": { ... },
+  "metrics": [ ... ],
+  "passed": true,
+  "thresholds": [
+    { "metric": "exact_match", "min": 0.9, "score": 0.95, "passed": true },
+    { "metric": "toxicity", "min": 0.95, "score": 1.0, "passed": true }
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+#### Markdown (when thresholds specified)
+```markdown
+## Thresholds
+
+- **exact_match:** PASS (min: 0.9, actual: 0.95)
+- **toxicity:** PASS (min: 0.95, actual: 1.0)
+```
+
+## SDK Usage
+
+```javascript
+import { Eval } from 'frai-core';
+
+const evaluations = Eval.runEvaluations({ outputs, references });
+
+const report = Eval.generateReport({
+  evaluations,
+  outputsPath: 'outputs.json',
+  referencesPath: 'references.json',
+  thresholds: {
+    exact_match: 0.9,
+    toxicity: 0.95
+  }
+});
+
+if (report.passed === false) {
+  console.error('Failed thresholds:', report.thresholds);
+  process.exit(1);
+}
+```
+
+## Custom Metrics Support
+
+Thresholds work with any custom metric as long as the metric object has an `id` field and `score` property:
+
+```javascript
+const customMetrics = [
+  {
+    id: 'my_metric',
+    label: 'My Custom Metric',
+    score: 0.85,
+    // ... other properties
+  }
+];
+
+const report = Eval.generateReport({
+  evaluations: customMetrics,
+  thresholds: { my_metric: 0.8 }
+});
+// report.passed will be true since 0.85 >= 0.8
+```
+
+## Backward Compatibility
+
+- Without `--threshold` option, behavior is identical to before
+- Reports without thresholds do not have `passed` or `thresholds` fields
+- Exit codes are 0 for success (unchanged)
+- All existing tests continue to pass
